{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Adoption Maturity Model.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Adoption Maturity Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai adoption maturity model ai adoption maturity model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI Adoption Maturity Model.md","fileName":"AI Adoption Maturity Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI Adoption Maturity Model","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps AI Governance]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps AI Governance","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Adoption Maturity Model.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Adoption Maturity Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai adoption maturity model ai adoption maturity model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI Adoption Maturity Model.md","fileName":"AI Adoption Maturity Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI Adoption Maturity Model","heading":"AI Adoption Maturity Model","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The AI adoption maturity model describes a progression from informal use to enterprise optimization. Early experimentation establishes capability; defined guardrails constrain it; enforced approval controls consequential work; auditing and compliance make participation provable; and optimized adoption uses evidence to refine cost, quality, and scale.\n\nMaturity is not the number of AI tools deployed. It is the degree to which use is bounded, reviewed, traceable, and connected to organizational outcomes. Teams should expand only after the previous level's controls are effective, rather than treating broad access as proof of readiness.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps AI Governance","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"p